	(text "RC CHARGE-PUMP WATCHDOG\n\n- WD_OK active HIGH\n- WDI HIGH->LOW transition pets the dog\n\nFirmware toggles WDI in software (50-1000 Hz, ~50% duty) only while the control loop is healthy.\nNever drive WDI from a timer/PWM: a timer keeps running after the CPU hangs.\nEach falling edge on WDI pulls the Q24 gate low through C169 and tops up C170 via R178.\nWD_OK ~2.7 V while toggling. WDI stuck high, low or floating: <1 V in ~100 ms, <0.4 V in ~190 ms\n(10 uF nominal; DC-bias derating shortens this). WD_OK starts at 0 V at power-up (fail-safe).\nWD_OK drives N-FET gates only (14.4 V rail switch, LiDAR incl. laser): no resistive loads.\nWDI pin: high-Z at reset, no pull-down."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 70.104 126.746 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
